SWEET nav tap hold + thread wait witness (patch 0249, T-10ba, G-10b-nav; R0 log only, no register or memory write outside the patch's own statics): (1) the SweetHIDTouch nav session (0243/0247) held every tap as a 100 ms drag from its (x0,y0) to the unused (x1,y1) = (0,0) of the table row and lifted the finger at 0,0 (observed: 12 'SWEET HID: touch 0 up at 0,0' lines in run 20261107T230750Z-gputest-nav3), so iOS never saw a tap and no app launched; a kind 0 action now holds the finger at (x0,y0) for all ticks and lifts it there, and logs 'SWEET NAV: tap hold X,Y ticks N' at the up event (swipes and waits unchanged); (2) boot-arg sweetthrwait=N (N ms, clamped to 2..50, default off: no thread, nothing printed; sweetthrcpu stays as it is) starts a second kernel thread (bsd/dev/sweet_thrwait.c, sweet_thrwait_start next to sweet_thrcpu_start in sweet_ufs, bsd/conf/files) that samples every thread of backboardd and SpringBoard every N ms under task_lock + splsched/thread_lock (sweet_thrwait_task and sweet_thrwait_slide in osfmk/kern/exception.c): thread->state, and for a TH_WAIT thread block_hint, wait_event and the user pc/lr of find_user_regs, read from the thread structure only (nothing the event or a port points to, no copyin), aggregated in a 512-entry static table keyed (pid, tid, hint, event, pc, lr), printed once per second as 'SWEET THRWAIT: t NS samples S waiting W running R entries E dropped D' plus up to 24 'SWEET THRWAIT: pid P tid T idx I hint H ev E pc PC lr LR n N' rows, 'SWEET THRWAIT: pid P slide S' once per process, loud one-time lines for a process not found / without a task / over 256 threads / a full table (dropped), 60000 lines per boot then 'cap reached'.
